
# StoryVerse Development Log

Last updated: 16 November 2026

## 1. Project vision
StoryVerse is a premium reading and writing application combining an immersive digital library, customizable reader and intelligent authoring studio.

## 2. Main navigation
- Home
- Library
- Discover
- Create
- Profile

## 3. Reader features
- Import EPUB, PDF and TXT files initially.
- Read offline.
- Customize fonts, sizes, spacing, colours and backgrounds.
- Look up words without leaving the page.
- Get explanations of selected passages.
- Save bookmarks, notes, vocabulary and reading progress.
- Discover legally available free books and legitimate purchase links.

## 4. Author Studio
- Create and manage separate story projects.
- Organize characters, worlds, settings, plots and timelines.
- Plan chapters, scenes, arcs and backstories.
- Write and edit manuscripts.
- Search project information.
- Use an AI assistant that distinguishes established story canon from new suggestions.
- Autosave work.

## 5. Visual direction
Create an original cinematic, premium interface with atmospheric depth, beautiful book covers, elegant cards and purposeful motion.

Both Dark Mode and Light Mode must be carefully designed. The reader should be calm and distraction-free.

## 6. Technical direction
- Flutter.
- Android first, with a responsive web preview.
- Local-first and offline-first architecture.
- Local database and persistent storage.
- Optional AI services behind a replaceable integration layer.
- Never host unauthorized copyrighted books.

## 7. Existing prototype
Build 02 was previously prepared outside this repository.

It includes:
- Five-tab navigation.
- Home screen.
- Library screen with sample search and filters.
- Discover screen.
- Create screen.
- Profile and theme settings.
- Light, Dark and System themes.

Important: these are prototype screens. File importing, real book reading, project persistence and online discovery are not yet implemented.

## 8. Development roadmap
1. Establish the GitHub project structure.
2. Add the Flutter starter source.
3. Configure Flutter Web.
